Apple today added an "Intelligent Assistant" to Keynote, Numbers, and Pages. The feature is available in beta for Apple Creator Studio subscribers. The update is available again following <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/22/apple-removes-iwork-apps-app-store/">the temporary removal</a> of the apps from the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/app-store/">App Store</a>. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-keynote.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072252" /><br/>
In Numbers, Intelligent Assistant can build formulas, visualize data, help generate formulas with natural language, and generate tables.<br/>
<br/>
The Pages Intelligent Assistant can start a first draft, and "edit, organize, and elevate your writing." It can draft sections, adjust tone, and generate images or shapes using natural language.<br/>
<br/>
With Keynote, Intelligent Assistant can help build and refine slides, add animations, create presenter notes, and generate images and shapes.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-numbers.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072253" /><br/>
For all three apps, Intelligent Assistant can search for information on a topic on the web and then add it to a document. Apple says Intelligent Assistant can also walk users through using advanced features or make suggestions on what to try.<br/>
<br/>
Along with Intelligent Assistant, Creator Studio subscribers also have access to new templates and themes, as well as curated videos that can be found in the Content Hub.<br/>
<br/>
For all users, the apps include bug fixes and performance improvements. Keynote also has an Interchange Format for importing and exporting presentations.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/iphone-duo-pages.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072254" /><br/>
Though not mentioned in the release notes, the updates also add <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> support to all three apps.<br/>
<br/>
